# Every environment variable Stemma reads. Names only: never commit values.
#
# Nothing loads a .env file: export these in the shell that runs Stemma (for example
# `set -a; . ./.env; set +a`), or pass the file to Docker with --env-file. Copy this file
# to .env (ignored by git) and uncomment only the lines you set: an empty value is not
# the same as unset (an empty STEMMA_DATALAYER is refused, and with Docker an empty line
# overrides the image's defaults). Keep each value on its own line with no trailing
# comment, since Docker reads everything after "=" as the value.

# --- Runs (needed for a live run) ---
# Absolute path where run folders are written (outside the repository).
# STEMMA_RUNS=
# Absolute path of the request-keyed fetch cache (outside the repository). Optional.
# STEMMA_CACHE=
# Interpreter with Stemma installed, used by hooks and analysis scripts.
# Default: the interpreter running Stemma.
# STEMMA_PYTHON=
# The pinned Claude Code binary (2.1.308), for example installed with
#   npm install --prefix <tools>/claude-code-2.1.308 @anthropic-ai/claude-code@2.1.308
# STEMMA_CLAUDE_BIN=
# A signed-in Claude Code configuration folder used only for runs (see below).
# STEMMA_CLAUDE_CONFIG=
# "Name email": the contact SEC requires in the User-Agent. Set at run time only.
# STEMMA_SEC_IDENTITY=

# Making STEMMA_CLAUDE_CONFIG: create an empty folder, run the pinned binary once
# interactively with CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR set to that folder, and sign in. Add nothing else
# (no CLAUDE.md, skills, plugins or memory). Every session uses this one folder, because
# the sign-in is keyed to it; a copy of the folder is not signed in. Each launch passes
# settings that switch off claude.ai-synced plugins, connectors and bundled skills
# (src/stemma/driver/settings.py).

# --- Demo ---
# true: `python run.py` replays the recorded sample instead of running live.
# SAMPLE_MODE=

# --- Data layer (optional; the default, sqlite, needs nothing) ---
# sqlite (default) or zetaris.
# STEMMA_DATALAYER=
# sqlite (default; logged) or none.
# STEMMA_DATALAYER_FALLBACK=
# Default http://localhost:8888/api/v1.0
# ZETARIS_REST_URL=
# Created in the Zetaris web console under Management, API Tokens.
# ZETARIS_API_KEY=
# Default 1.
# ZETARIS_ORG_ID=
# Default lightning.metastore.stemma
# STEMMA_ZETARIS_NAMESPACE=
# The evidence Postgres. Defaults: 127.0.0.1, 5544, stemma, stemma (the owning role).
# STEMMA_PG_HOST=
# STEMMA_PG_PORT=
# STEMMA_PG_DB=
# STEMMA_PG_USER=
# The owning role's password.
# STEMMA_PG_PASSWORD=
# The Postgres host name as Zetaris sees it. Default stemma-evidence-pg
# STEMMA_PG_JDBC_HOST=
# Folder outside the repository holding the Zetaris bundle, its install log and its
# secrets; used by hackathon/zetaris/finish-install.sh. No default: unset is an error.
# STEMMA_ZETARIS_HOME=

# --- Nightshift provider client (optional) ---
# Default http://127.0.0.1:8088/v1
# METERLESS_BASE_URL=
# The runtime token, or set METERLESS_STATE_DIR to read <dir>/proxy-token instead.
# METERLESS_RUNTIME_TOKEN=
# METERLESS_STATE_DIR=

# --- Tests only ---
# 1 runs the live evidence tests, which reach public web sites.
# STEMMA_LIVE=
# Folder for the live tests' JSON summaries. Default: a temporary folder.
# STEMMA_LIVE_OUT=

# Set by Stemma for its own sessions, or by the conformance scripts; never set these:
# STEMMA_RUN_DIR, STEMMA_ANALYSIS_INPUTS, STEMMA_ANALYSIS_RESULT, STEMMA_ANALYSIS_DOCUMENTS,
# STEMMA_WM_MEMORY_AS_FILE.
